  "goodToKnow": "Ehrenamtlich means voluntary or unpaid, for work done out of public spirit: ehrenamtlich tätig sein. Das Ehrenamt is voluntary work, and German life depends on it: volunteer fire brigades (Freiwillige Feuerwehr) cover most of the country, coaches run sports clubs, and helpers staff the Tafeln (food banks). Studies show around a third or more of Germans volunteer. Literally, it's an office (Amt) held for honour (Ehre), not money."
